.Dd June 2026
.Dt UNBFC 1
.Os bfcodec 0.0.6
.Sh NAME
.Nm unbfc
.Nd decrypt a file in place with BFCodec
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl V
.Nm
.Op Fl K Ar key | Fl -key Ar key | Fl -key-file Ar path | Fl -uuid Ar uuid
.Op Fl -iv Ar iv | Fl -iv-file Ar path
.Op Fl -backup
.Op Fl o Ar path
.Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
decrypts a
.Ar file
that was produced by
.Xr bfc 1 ,
overwriting
.Ar file
with the result, or writing to the path given by
.Fl o
if present.
The 8-byte trailer appended by
.Xr bfc 1
is used to restore the exact original size after decryption.
.Pp
The key and IV must match those used to encrypt the file.
If no key is given, a default passphrase is used; if no IV is given, a default
IV is used.
The key can be given as a passphrase
.Pq Fl K Ns / Ns Fl -key ,
which is MD5-hashed to 16 bytes, as a raw binary file
.Pq Fl -key-file ,
or as a device UUID
.Pq Fl -uuid ,
whose canonical uppercase form is MD5-hashed to 16 bytes.
The IV can be given as hex
.Pq Fl -iv ;
spaces are ignored.
The IV in hex is 16 hex digits (8 bytes).
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl V
Print version and exit.
.It Fl K , Fl -key Ar key
Passphrase, MD5-hashed to 16 bytes for the key.
Default is the passphrase for jubeat Plus.
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl -key-file .
.It Fl -key-file Ar path
Read the key from the binary file
.Ar path
(first 16 bytes used; file may be longer).
Overrides the default passphrase.
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl -key .
.It Fl -uuid Ar uuid
Device UUID; its canonical uppercase
.Sq 8-4-4-4-12
form is MD5-hashed to 16 bytes for the key.
Dashes and letter case are optional.
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl K , Fl -key , and Fl -key-file .
.It Fl -iv Ar iv
IV as 16 hex digits (8 bytes); spaces ignored.
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl -iv-file .
A default IV is used if neither
.Fl -iv
nor
.Fl -iv-file
is given.
.It Fl -iv-file Ar path
Read the IV from the binary file
.Ar path
(first 8 bytes used; file may be longer).
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl -iv .
.It Fl -backup
Back up the destination to
.Ar dest Ns .bak
before overwriting it, if the destination already exists.
.It Fl o , Fl -output Ar path
Write the output to
.Ar path
instead of overwriting the input.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bfc 1 ,
.Xr jbt 1 ,
.Xr unjbt 1
